      "id": 1,
      "text": "Richmond Hill's Victorian architecture and tree‑lined streets make it one of Queens’ most architecturally cohesive neighborhoods.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityneighborhoods.nyc/richmond-hill",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Richmond Hill Historical Society, founded in 1999, preserves the area’s late‑19th‑century homes and civic landmarks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        4,
        6,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.richmondhillhistory.org/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A former movie theater, RKO Keith’s Richmond Hill Theater, opened in 1929 and now serves as a bingo hall.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richmond_Hill%2C_Queens",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s name comes from a hill that was once part of the Welling Farm, later renamed Jamaica under British rule.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richmond_Hill%2C_Queens",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Richmond Hill once hosted a Long Island Rail Road station on the Montauk Branch, helping spur early residential development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richmond_Hill%2C_Queens",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The area was home to Yankees Hall of Famer Phil Rizzuto, who attended high school in Richmond Hill.",
